WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:22.840
Hey, this is really interesting.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.990
There's a few Republican governors who have
been ignoring, if not completely abandoning

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.550
Donald Trump when it comes to dealing with
the virus in their states.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.680
And their popularity has absolutely exploded.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.290
I'm talking mostly about Ohio Republican Governor
Mike DeWine.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:44.070
He's done a pretty good job of handling Corona
virus from day one, although more recently

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.170
there are some concerns about the policies
he's rolling out.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:52.130
But he's mostly been following health experts
and not Donald Trump and his popularity has

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.220
soared.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:57.810
We also have been looking at how Maryland
Republican Governor Larry Hogan has been dealing

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.810
with the virus.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:03.800
And then our own governor here in Massachusetts,
Charlie Baker, a Republican as well, has been

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.280
doing a pretty good job.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:11.469
And the reason that we care about this is
that the November of 2020 elections are in

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:14.240
many ways referendums.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.240
That's the way.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.240
It's not referenda.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.990
I looked it up, referendums on Donald Trump.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:24.390
When we look at the Senate race in North Carolina
with Republican Thom Tillis or we look at

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:30.149
Martha McSally in Arizona, or you look at
Susan Collins in Maine, these are in large

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:33.009
part adjudications of the Trump regime.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:36.490
And so far, it's not going particularly well
for those Republicans.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:42.490
Many Republicans have been afraid of contradicting
or crossing Donald Trump because they're afraid

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.749
it might be bad for their local and state
races.

00:01:44.749 --> 00:01:45.920
Trump might target me.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.439
It could be really, really bad.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:52.369
But what we're seeing is that Ohio Republican
Governor Mike DeWine has absolutely split

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:58.430
from Trump and he is hugely benefiting from
it in terms of approval, in terms of popularity.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:01.520
And this may be a signal for twenty, twenty
six months away.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.860
We can't say for sure, but it may be a signal.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.409
What did Mike DeWine do?

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:10.100
Mike DeWine lockdown down Ohio early before
other Republicans took it seriously, before

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.840
Donald Trump was even taking it seriously.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.620
He's been doing regular briefings that are
actually fact based and they attract Democrats

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:20.140
and Republicans in Ohio and even nationally.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.510
People are watching these, much like Andrew
Cuomo's briefings.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:28.760
Conservative activists and business leaders
have been pressuring DeWine to do what Trump

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.150
wants, start reopening, do all this stuff.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.490
And DeWine just hasn't done it.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.880
And he's been listening to the health experts.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.390
He also came out in favor of a mail in primary
late last month.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:45.510
Trump has been viciously opposed to mail in
voting and then more recently this week.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:51.300
DeWine has started to loosen up some of the
guidelines as businesses can start opening.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.760
Masks are recommended six feet, separation
is recommended for workers and customers.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:03.040
And for a while before this, 30 or more Republicans
in the state legislature were demanding that

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:06.530
DeWine open everything right away and he didn't
do it.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:12.150
Living with Trump and his approval on Corona
virus is 85 percent.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:18.040
His trustworthiness rating is eighty nine
percent on Corona virus.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.230
You don't get those numbers with just Republicans.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.010
He's taking testing seriously.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.990
He says they're going to roughly triple testing
by the end of the month in Ohio from 7000

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.130
a day to 20000 a day.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:36.400
And what's interesting is that when we look
at Maryland and Massachusetts, Republican

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:43.320
governors in blue states, you kind of have
to, as a Republican governor, follow what

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:47.100
your liberal state legislatures want you to
do.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:51.950
Massachusetts has a Republican governor and
Charlie Baker, but a very left legislature

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.390
and a relatively left voting public.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.120
So it's not surprising that Charlie Baker
is doing more.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.860
What our state wants rather than what Trump
wants.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.030
But Ohio, it's certainly a battleground state.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:04.610
But it's not a left wing stronghold of any
kind.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:08.460
So you might imagine that what Mike DeWine
has done in abandoning Trump would be far

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.020
more risky, but it has worked here in Massachusetts.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:15.580
Charlie Baker, former CEO of a big health
insurance company.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.079
I didn't vote for him.

00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:22.230
I'm not looking to have more and more governors
be former CEOs of health insurance companies.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.360
But Charlie Baker knows how to delegate.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.860
He knows how to trust experts and he knows
how to look at data.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:32.189
Remember that Dr. Burke's laughably claimed
that Trump looks at data and makes decisions

00:04:32.189 --> 00:04:33.979
by assimilating the information.

00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:36.120
We all knew it was B.S..

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.770
What we want to see is governors actually
do what the wine has been doing.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:44.000
To some degree, what Charlie Baker and Hogan
have been doing.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.919
I'm hopeful that as a result, on May 18th
here in Massachusetts, Charlie Baker will

00:04:48.919 --> 00:04:51.930
be able to announce some loosening of certain
guidelines.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.470
If the numbers keep improving.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:57.300
Yesterday here in Massachusetts, we had only
1.4 percent case growth.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.550
That's really low.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.569
We had a week of about 3 percent daily case
growth.

00:05:01.569 --> 00:05:03.250
That's really not bad.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:04.949
So competence is important.

00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:07.120
Ideology is less important here.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:12.960
Armed protesters aside, for the most part,
we've seen people across the country approve

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.990
of competence, even across party lines.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:20.650
Massachusetts voters overwhelmingly pleased
with Republican Charlie Baker despite being

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:21.750
a blue state.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:28.349
Ohio voters, Democrats and Republicans, nearly
90 percent approval on a corona virus.

00:05:28.349 --> 00:05:33.120
Trustworthiness for the Republican governor
who has abandoned the doctrine of Donald Trump.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:38.430
Again, this may be a big signal for how November
of 2020 may go.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.070
Hopefully, we don't know.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.870
We've got to count every single vote.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.970
We have to cast every ballot.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:46.629
But that is the upside to what we are seeing.

00:05:46.629 --> 00:05:51.590
We'll have continued coverage of this on the
David Pakman show Instagram page at David

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:53.099
Pakman show.

00:05:53.099 --> 00:05:54.289
Follow me while you're there at Davis.

